    "<div>\n          <h3>\n            <span></span>\n            PART C: READING ( 2,6 POINTS)\n          </h3>\n          <span>Kỹ Năng Đọc Hiểu</span>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section I: Cloze Passage -->\n        <div>\n          <div>\n            <h4>\n              I. Choose the correct answer A, B, C or D to fill in each blank in the following passage. (1.0 points)\n            </h4>\n          </div>\n\n          <div>\n            <p>\n              Leisure activities are very important to people. There are a lot of activities they can do in their free time. The most (1) ______ type of leisure activities are those that are done just for fun. Often these activities do not need a special skill in order to do them. In many parts of the world, (2) ______ television is the number one leisure activity. Other popular choices include talking (3) ______ friends, eating out, playing sports, travelling, and playing electronic games.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              More serious leisure activities include working on a hobby, such as building a model plane or working with pottery. People need to (4) ______ a special skill or have experience to do these types of leisure activities.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Leisure brings different rewards to different people. People usually feel happy and relaxed (5) ______ doing their leisure activities. They can also feel a sense of adventure and pride in their accomplishment.\n            </p>\n          </div>\n\n          <!-- Cloze Questions 1-5 -->\n          <div>\n            <!-- Q1 -->\n            \n\n            <!-- Q2 -->\n            \n\n            <!-- Q3 -->\n            \n\n            <!-- Q4 -->\n            \n\n            <!-- Q5 -->\n            \n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section II: Reading Comprehension -->\n        <div>\n          <div>\n            <h4>\n              II. Read the text and do the tasks below. (1.6 pts)\n            </h4>\n          </div>\n\n          <div>\n            <p>\n              A lot of teenagers take part in clubs in their schools. So what are the benefits of school clubs?\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              First, when you join a school club you make new friends. You will meet other students who could potentially become your new close friends. The reason is that clubs have members with something in common. At club meetings you will spend some time with other members. This will help you better understand one another and even become friends.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              In addition, being a club member helps you learn new skills. By participating in different clubs and working with diverse people, you can develop such skills as communication, teamwork, and time management.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Another benefit of joining a club is that you can improve yourself. You not only learn more about your area of interest but you can also become more confident. You will have a chance to work with new people, organize club activities, and take part in different events. This will make you feel much better about yourself.\n            </p>\n          </div>\n\n          <!-- Task A: Open Questions -->\n          <div>\n            <h5>Answer the questions: (0,4points)</h5>\n\n            <!-- Q1 -->\n            \n\n            <!-- Q2 -->\n            \n\n            <!-- Q3 -->\n            \n          </div>\n\n          <!-- Task B: MC Questions -->\n          <div>\n            <h5>B. Choose the best answer A, B, C or D to complete the sentences (0,4 points)</h5>\n\n            <!-- Q4 (Phrases / sentences - no audio before submit) -->\n            \n\n            <!-- Q5 (Short phrases - neutral audio enabled) -->\n            \n          </div>\n        </div>",
